# Paths `semgrep scan` skips. A root .semgrepignore replaces Semgrep's built-in list
# (src/targeting/default.semgrepignore in semgrep/semgrep), so its entries are repeated here, except one:
# Semgrep skips test/ and tests/ by default, but tests follow the same standards (JAVA-3, JAVA-14, GEN-6),
# so they are scanned too. Semgrep also skips files git doesn't track (target/, coverage/, ...).

# Version control
.git
.svn
.hg

# Build output and vendored code
build/
vendor/
dist/
*.min.js

# Package managers
node_modules/
.npm/
.yarn/
.venv/

# Rule fixtures contain the flagged patterns on purpose; `semgrep --test .semgrep` checks them instead.
.semgrep/
